// §5.7, on analog procedural assignments: "Concatenation expressions cannot be
// used as part of the analog_expression (assigning to list of values in the
// analog context is not allowed)."
//
// Read where that sentence points: the analog_expression is the RIGHT of the
// `=`. The concatenation here is on the LEFT, and what forbids it is Syntax 5-7
// itself — analog_variable_lvalue is a variable_identifier or an indexed
// element of one, with no concatenation alternative. Either way the reason is
// the parenthetical's: a concatenation names an ordered bundle of values, not a
// storage location, so there is nothing to assign to.
// procedural_assignments.va is the positive §5.7 fixture and keeps compiling.
//
//! lrm 5.7
//! lrm A.8.5
//! reject E0317
module ch5_assignment_concatenation(p);
  inout p; electrical p; real x, y;
  analog begin
    {x, y} = 1.0;
    I(p) <+ x;
  end
endmodule
